WEBVTT

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:28.780
Bring in the prisoner, conspiring against the Klingon Empire, how do you respawn?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.740
I'm not guilty.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.950
When this tribunal convenes tomorrow,

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.670
you will be given a chance to prove your innocence.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:41.640
If you cannot, there is only one punishment.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:15.810
getting from there to here been a long time my time is fine i will see my dream come alive at last

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:26.660
touch the sky not gonna hold me down no more no they're not gonna change my mind

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:43.410
Five minutes.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:47.740
Glad you could drop by.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:48.770
Are you?

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:50.970
Been better.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:53.590
Sure if I find you alive.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.510
They promised me a trial before the execution.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:02:59.720
You're wrong.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.460
You know, Paul, this athemia can be highly contagious.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.840
I'm surprised they haven't put you in isolation.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.000
Any residual symptoms?

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.460
Fever? Dizziness?

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.080
Just a scratchy throat.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.180
Let's have a look.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:19.170
Get here.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.640
Two days ago, but they refused to let us see you.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.540
Enemies of the state aren't allowed visitors.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:29.900
Paul was finally able to convince them that your condition necessitated a visit from your doctor.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.780
Very thoughtful of her.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:37.870
She sends her regards, and she wanted me to assure you that Starfleet and the Vulcan High Command are doing everything possible to get you released.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.180
Aren't they having any luck?

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:45.720
Not yet. But she and Commander Tucker have begun exploring other options for regaining your freedom.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:57.740
It's over the outcome. Counting on them to get Enterprise safely out of Klingon territory.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:04.720
How are your accommodations?

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:08.290
So bad.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:12.000
Can't say I'm a big fan of Klingon cuisine.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:16.080
It may not appear appetizing, but it seems like a good source of protein.

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:17.610
I suggest you eat it.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:21.790
Is he infectious?

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.300
I don't believe so.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.060
Then return to your ship.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:26.650
I'd like to run some more tests.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.270
You're not here to treat him.

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:35.470
Thanks for the house call, Doc.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.180
I'm sure I'll see you soon.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.920
I'm Kolos, your advocate.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:44.960
Jonathan Archer.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:48.440
Tribunal's about to begin.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.880
We haven't even discussed what happened.

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:52.650
I'm familiar with the charges.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.930
Well, I'm not familiar with your justice system.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.290
What can I expect out there?

00:04:58.910 --> 00:04:59.970
Now that you've been charged.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.100
The evidence against you will be presented.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:03.900
Do I get a chance to testify?

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:07.340
I will conduct your defense.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:11.120
How can you do that when you haven't heard what really happened?

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:13.550
I know what happened.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.940
You mustn't speak during the tribunal.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:18.710
I'll speak for you.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:47.420
I'm saying, enemy, they're not the jury.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:49.520
There is no jury.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:01.710
Who's that?

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:03.700
Prosecutor Auroch.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.110
The success is welcome.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.080
What about you?

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:10.830
What's your success rate?

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:14.710
As before, Ibuji.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:26.300
Ibuji.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:26.860
Ibuji is convened.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:29.060
Strength to the Empire.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.200
Prosecutor Horak, you may proceed.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:35.970
I call Duras, son of Toral.

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:46.350
Captain Duras, tell the tribunal about your encounter with the accused.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:48.030
I am no longer a captain.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:49.640
Explain.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:55.610
I am a second weapons officer serving on the Thai Gokor defense perimeter.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:59.970
The Duras I called to testify is commander of the battlecruiser Bork.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.600
I was recently reduced in rank.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:09.850
A distinguished Klingon warrior, stripped of his command.

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:13.470
Did the accused have anything to do with your disgrace?

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:15.200
Yes.

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:19.420
Go on, weapons officer Duras.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:25.040
A group of rebels had fled the Klingon protectorate at Rod Duras.

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:27.960
I was commanded to bring these traitors to justice.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:29.960
We'd followed their...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.180
warp trail to a system just outside Klingon territory they're near the fifth planet another

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:45.280
vessel is docked with them show me kind of ship is that unknown but they've taken the rebels aboard

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:52.320
armaments torpedo launch is far and aft low-yield particle cannons we can defeat them easily

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:59.920
intercept they're signaling us viewer and defy your

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.420
Captain Archer of the Battlecruiser Enterprise.

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:08.010
The people aboard your ship are wanted for treason. Surrender them immediately.

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:09.590
By whose authority?

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:11.960
Chancellor of the Klingon High Council.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:15.320
I don't know your Chancellor, and I don't give a damn what he wants.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.860
I've formed an alliance with these people, and I'm going to support their revolt.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:22.240
Give them to me now, or I'll destroy your vessel.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:26.750
Fire one shot, and you'll be joining your ancestors in the afterlife.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.980
He refused to surrender.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.250
Yes.

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.240
I didn't say any of those things.

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:35.550
Can't you object?

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:37.480
It's not important.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:41.570
How did you respond to Archer's defiance?

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:43.710
Pityed him.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:47.860
He was about to die in defense of these wretched traitors.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:49.040
They weren't traitors.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:54.510
I, Bucket, haven't you informed the prisoner of the rules of this tribunal?

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.510
My apologies, Magister.

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:57.910
But silent.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:08:59.600
You will be removed.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:08.480
continue i showed him more patience than he deserved but obviously he wanted blood to be

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:16.110
spilled don't be a fool your ship is inferior you won't survivable with us death to the empire

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:52.170
system the coward thinks he can hide pursue them he's interfering with sensors

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:46.230
three hours to repair our warp drive.

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:48.740
But of course by that time they were gone.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.640
But fortunate your first officer didn't kill you

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.180
for such a failure, you're dismissed.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:02.820
You're not going to question him?

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:05.510
He'd say nothing that would help you.

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:08.430
Do you have any further evidence to present?

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.210
No, Magistrate.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:13.180
Durot's testimony is clear.

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:15.880
He was attempting to carry out his mission,

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:20.440
to bring enemies of the Empire to justice.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:24.300
But this aggressor, this human,

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:28.380
conspired with them to disgrace a proud warrior

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:29.840
and foment rebellion.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:34.740
There can be no doubt that he is our enemy as well.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:40.040
Martin Archer claims to be innocent.

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:41.810
Innocent or what?

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:48.680
The tribunal has already been far too lenient.

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:52.780
We haven't accused his crew or his government.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:57.400
He's fortunate we haven't dispatched a fleet of warships to his home world.

00:11:57.760 --> 00:11:59.980
But we do demand that he be held responsible.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:07.040
For the crimes he has committed we demand that he received the most severe punishment our laws decree

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:29.960
No magistrate

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.880
Then I will consider the evidence and deliver my verdict.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.440
I'd like a chance to defend myself.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:37.320
You have been warned.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.540
He's distorting the truth.

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:39.540
Be silent!

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:41.120
Those people weren't rebels,

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:43.230
and I wasn't trying to start a rebellion.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.270
I am not your enemy.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:52.560
Tribunal is in recess.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:31.910
What is this?

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:33.740
Targ.

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:35.810
It's a little underdone.

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:39.380
I told you to remain silent.

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:40.240
You should have listened to me.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:43.440
Sorry if I interfered with your legal strategy.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:46.280
My strategy may yet spare your life.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.440
I've spoken with the magistrate

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:50.660
who's willing to show you mercy if you cooperate.

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:51.700
Oh.

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:53.690
Tell him where to find the rebels.

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:56.890
Told you, they're not rebels.

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:59.250
Doesn't matter what you believe.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:13:59.960
They're some .

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.800
There's nothing you can say that will change that.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:04.840
I haven't been able to say anything.

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:08.030
Where did you take them?

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:11.540
Another ship? Planet?

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.690
Understand what will happen if you don't tell them.

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:18.760
I did.

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:22.120
I'm offering you a way to save your life.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:26.620
Let's say I did cooperate.

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:29.660
What would happen to these people?

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:32.970
They would be charged with treason.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.330
And end up in a court like this one?

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:41.450
Magistrate I'm going to pass on his offer.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:48.260
Fool. Sacrifice himself for people he barely knows.

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:49.400
I know them well enough.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.880
They're good people, and I won't turn them over.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:56.190
If you'd let me testify, tell my side of the story,

00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:58.650
it might become clear why I helped them.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:14:59.980
But from what I've seen...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.660
you're all perfectly happy to ignore what you don't want to hear.

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:07.830
Don't be so quick to accuse me of sharing their interpretation of the law.

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:11.220
No? What's your interpretation?

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:14.790
I became an advocate many years ago.

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:18.260
They were different times.

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:20.830
Better or worse?

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:23.260
The courts were more willing to listen.

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:29.590
Then maybe you should remind them of those different times.

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:32.530
Nothing like a good history lesson.

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:42.220
Challenge the rules.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.810
Even if your client's life depends on it,

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:48.960
I get the feeling you're as frustrated as I am.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.710
That you want to stand up to them.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:55.940
You've given up.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:57.520
You're afraid of them.

00:15:58.070 --> 00:15:59.050
Not afraid.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:15:59.910
Then prove it.

00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:04.460
Challenge them. Show them what a real trial is like.

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:31.900
Strength to the Empire.

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:36.700
Did you inform the accused of our offer?

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:37.620
I have.

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:40.340
And does he wish to address this tribunal?

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:41.160
He does.

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:44.620
He wishes to testify in his own defense.

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:45.320
I object.

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:47.490
The time for testimony is over.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:50.630
With respect, magistrate, no verdict has been reached.

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:51.470
Irrelevant!

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:53.410
I urge you to end these proceedings.

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:56.310
I am within my rights to present further testimony.

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:58.690
You're speaking of archaic rights.

00:16:59.140 --> 00:16:59.960
Surely I don't...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.700
I don't need to remind the Magistrate.

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:04.000
The Judicial Charter of Koloth states,

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:06.880
an advocate is entitled to challenge the charges

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.720
at any point during the tribunal.

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:12.790
To my knowledge, a charter has not been cast aside.

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:18.600
From the time of Kalos, our courts have stood as a forum

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:21.690
where justice is dispensed with honor!

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:22.420
Honor!

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:27.270
Now, will my case be heard or will it not?

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:47.330
call your witness identify yourself i'm captain jonathan archer of the earth starship enterprise

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:53.580
do you admit captain archer that you gave aid and comfort to a vessel fleeing the empire

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:59.100
we answered a distress call they were starving their life support was failing

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:03.180
Isn't that issue here? You helped them to escape.

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:06.550
Will my client be allowed to testify or not?

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:13.580
Prosecutor, you will show the advocate the same respect he has shown you. Continue.

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:18.990
Account for this tribunal your recollection of the events.

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:22.830
As I said, we had received a distress call.

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:27.270
Magnify. Bioscience?

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:28.840
27.

00:18:32.140 --> 00:18:32.700
Any response?

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:35.220
No, sir.

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:40.210
Malcolm?

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:42.380
Main proportions offline.

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:44.350
Life support is failing.

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:46.470
Bad way, sir.

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:50.970
You duck with him?

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:54.160
Port engine is venting reactor coolant.

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:58.200
Try to come in on the starboard side, it'll be tricky.

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:01.080
Do your best.

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:07.960
Failed three weeks after we left.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:12.710
We tried to set a course for the nearest system at Impulse, but main power went down.

00:19:13.050 --> 00:19:15.020
How long ago was that?

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:19.340
I don't know. Six weeks. Maybe more.

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:23.900
We diverted auxiliary power to life support, but it wasn't enough.

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:27.980
Food processors failed. Water recyclers.

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:29.780
I've put them all on protein.

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:32.270
Two of them are in serious condition.

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:35.730
When we left, there were 54 aboard.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:38.330
Get you out here.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:44.160
Several years ago, our colony was annexed

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:46.440
by a species we had never seen before.

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:50.410
They said they'd provide for us in exchange for our allegiance,

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:52.910
that we'd become a part of their empire.

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:56.320
But they stripped us of our resources, left us with nothing.

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:58.760
We waited for them to return.

00:19:59.560 --> 00:19:59.980
They said...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.220
They'd bring food, fuel.

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:05.240
They never came back.

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.560
You knew they were fleeing the Empire.

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:11.460
We knew that their colony had been abandoned.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.760
And you chose to show them compassion.

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:16.000
They were starving.

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:18.360
They wouldn't have lasted another week.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:20.520
They were subjects of the Empire.

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:22.380
Their welfare was not your concern.

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:24.790
Apparently, it wasn't yours either.

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:29.160
You see the contempt these humans have for us.

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:29.980
He's still...

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:37.940
he did nothing wrong and prosecutor has yet to prove that he has he aided these rebels and now

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:57.700
he refuses to help us bring them to justice you will hear what the accused has to say my chief

00:20:57.700 --> 00:20:59.960
engineer had determined that their vessel was

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.040
beyond repair some of the crew will have to double up but I think we can

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:09.830
accommodate all of them I've already given the order considering the

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:15.900
alternative was to set the ship adrift I anticipated your decision where do you

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:19.940
plan to take them they were headed for a system a few light years from here but

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:24.510
you keep them safe from the Klingons empires tend to expand they may

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:28.780
eventually discover they haven't traveled far enough captain please report

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:29.200
to the bridge

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:41.470
They didn't abandon the colonists after all.

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:43.550
Perhaps they're bringing the supplies they promised.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:45.160
It's a D-5 battlecruiser.

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:46.700
I doubt it's bringing supplies.

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:49.720
How long before they get here?

00:21:51.020 --> 00:21:51.760
Seventeen minutes.

00:21:53.140 --> 00:21:54.220
Are all the refugees aboard?

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:55.080
Yes, sir.

00:21:57.060 --> 00:21:59.350
Cut their ship loose and go to tactical alert.

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:05.120
So, you were preparing for battle.

00:22:05.410 --> 00:22:07.190
I was preparing to defend my ship.

00:22:07.560 --> 00:22:09.820
As any good Klingon commander would be.

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:11.820
The accused has already admitted

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:14.300
that he knew the rebels were subjects of the Empire.

00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:16.460
They may have been subjects of the Empire,

00:22:16.540 --> 00:22:18.380
but it sure as hell looked like you had abandoned them.

00:22:18.560 --> 00:22:21.260
And he knew the Bortus was coming to retrieve them.

00:22:21.830 --> 00:22:23.650
Yet he launched a deliberate attack

